<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sokollu Mehmed Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1505">1505</a>–<a href="/years/1579">1579</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Mehmed-paša Sokolović, Sokollu Mehmet Paşa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sokollu Mehmed Pasha was an Ottoman statesman, grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> from 1565 to 1579 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-ii">Selim II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-iii">Murad III</a>. Born into an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian family in Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, he was taken as a boy through the devşirme and rose to be High Admiral of the Fleet, Governor-General of Rumelia and vizier. As grand vizier he kept Suleiman's death at Szigetvár secret in 1566 until Selim II could take power, made peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edirne">Edirne</a> in 1568 and rebuilt the fleet after Lepanto. He helped restore the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbian-patriarchate-of-pec">Serbian Patriarchate of Peć</a> in 1557, endowed the eleven-arched bridge at Višegrad and was assassinated on 11 October 1579.</p></div>
